PART3 = [('lykouris2021', 'Untrusted Predictions', 'S2.6', 'bounds the competitive ratio as a function of prediction error; we hold prediction accuracy fixed and move contention instead.'), ('antoniadis2022', 'Weighted Paging with Predictions', 'S2.6', 'uses predictions to beat the paging competitive ratio; our decision is whether to issue one call early, not which page to evict.'), ('karlin1990', 'Competitive analysis of paging', 'S2.6', 'is the classical competitive-analysis account of paging; our instrument is a simulation with intervals, not a worst-case bound.'), ('calibrated2025', 'Calibrated Machine Learning Predictions', 'S2.6', 'trusts a prediction in proportion to its calibration; we show a perfectly calibrated predictor still leaves a contention boundary to locate.'), ('predictionspecific2025', 'Prediction-Specific Design of Learning-Augmented Algorithms', 'S2.6', "designs algorithms around the prediction's own structure; our predictor is an oracle, so the fraction we report bounds any real predictor."), ('twoslope2025', 'two-slope ski rental', 'S2.6', 'controls tail risk in a two-slope ski-rental variant; our tail pair is a workload property rather than a decision-rule variant.'), ('multiagent2025', 'Multi-Agent Ski-Rental', 'S2.6', 'solves ski rental when several agents share a cost; several agents also share our worker pool, which is where the harm lands.'), ('improved2025', 'Improved Learning-Augmented Algorithms and (Tight) Lower Bounds', 'S2.6', 'gives tight lower bounds for learning-augmented problems; we report a measured boundary with a per-seed interval rather than a bound.'), ('waiting2025', 'Waiting is worth it and can be improved with predictions', 'S2.6', 'asks when waiting before acting is optimal; speculation is the dual decision, acting before the wait begins.'), ('discrete2026', 'Learning-Augmented Ski Rental with Discrete Distribution', 'S2.6', "uses a discrete distributional prediction for ski rental; our prediction's accuracy is fixed by construction, so the predictor is not the variable.", '10.1609/aaai.v40i43.40991'), ('parking2026', 'Parking Permit Problem', 'S2.6', 'gives primal-dual online algorithms for a rent-or-buy problem; our rent-or-buy is whether to pay for a call that may be discarded.'), ('kim2026', 'Robust and Consistent Ski Rental with Distributional Advice', 'S2.6', 'separates consistency from robustness under distributional advice; we report our confirmed and refuted priors in those same terms.'), ('cui2026', 'Ski Rental with Distributional Predictions of Unknown Quality', 'S2.6', 'handles predictions of unknown quality; our accuracy is known exactly because the simulator issues the predictions itself.'), ('canonne2025', 'With a Little Help From My Friends', 'S2.6', 'exploits probability distributions as advice in online problems; our advice is a random draw whose distribution we control.'), ('onlinegraph2022', 'Online Graph Algorithms with Predictions', 'S2.6', "carries predictions into online graph problems; our stream is an agent's own calls, whose order we also generate."), ('smoothness2023', 'Discrete-Smoothness in Online Algorithms with Predictions', 'S2.6', 'introduces discrete smoothness for prediction-augmented algorithms; we use a two-point tail pair rather than a smoothness parameter.'), ('newmetric2026', 'A new performance metric for the ski rental problem', 'S2.6', 'proposes a new metric for ski rental; our metric is a boundary in measured contention with a confidence interval.'), ('multishop2014', 'The multi-shop ski rental problem', 'S2.6', 'generalises rent-or-buy to several shops; our several-shop case is several workers sharing one pool.'), ('discount2022', 'Machine Learning Advised Ski Rental Problem with a Discount', 'S2.6', 'adds a discount to the advised ski-rental problem; our counterpart is a compensation cost charged on each missed prediction.'), ('advised2022', 'Machine learning advised algorithms for the ski rental problem', 'S2.6', 'advises the ski-rental decision with machine learning; we remove the learner and vary the load, isolating the contention channel.'), ('combinatorial2025', 'Combinatorial Ski Rental Problem', 'S2.6', 'extends ski rental to combinatorial decisions; our decision is one binary per step, priced by the pool.'), ('tailawarellm2026', 'Beyond Prediction: Tail-Aware Scheduling for LLM Inference', 'S2.6', 'schedules LLM inference using tail-aware prediction; we ask what that prediction buys when the pool, not the queue, is binding.'), ('lengthpred2026', 'Uncertainty-Aware Output Length Prediction', 'S2.6', "predicts output length with uncertainty for LLM scheduling; our instrument's predicted quantity is the call's duration, known exactly."), ('cnncost2026', 'Characterization-Guided Framework for CNN Inference Cost', 'S2.6', 'predicts inference cost from characterisation; cost prediction is the input our instrument assumes exact.'), ('calibrateroute2026', 'Calibrate, Then Route', 'S2.6', 'measures learned request routing after calibration; we show routing and early issue are different uses of the same prediction.'), ('eeckhout2025', 'Use Equal-Work or Equal-Time Speedup, Not Geomean Speedup', 'S2.7', 'argues geomean speedup misstates parallel gains; our headline is a ratio against the serial schedule of the same work.'), ('eeckhout2025b', 'R.I.P. Geomean Speedup', 'S2.7', 'shows geomean speedup is not a valid aggregate; we report per-cell intervals instead of an aggregate over cells.'), ('amdahl2013', "Computer Architecture and Amdahl's Law", 'S2.7', "re-reads Amdahl's law for modern architectures; our serial baseline is exactly the reference it requires."), ('amdahl2021', "On Extending Amdahl's law to Learn Computer Performance", 'S2.7', "extends Amdahl's law to learned performance models; we measure where the parallel fraction stops buying anything."), ('amdahl2026', "Modernizing Amdahl's Law", 'S2.7', "modernises Amdahl's law for AI scaling laws; our point is that part of a reported speculation gain was never serial work."), ('amdahl2026b', 'Scaling LLM Inference Beyond Amdahl', 'S2.7', "seeks speedups beyond Amdahl's limit by removing non-scalable work; we quantify how much of a reported speedup was already available."), ('amdahl2017', "How Amdahl's low restricts supercomputer applications", 'S2.7', "uses Amdahl's law to bound supercomputer applications; the same bound applies when the baseline is one agent's serial loop."), ('amdahl2017b', 'The Effect of Temperature on Amdahl Law', 'S2.7', "studies an environmental modifier of Amdahl's law; our modifier is contention rather than temperature, and it is measured."), ('amdahl2007', 'Parallel test description and analysis', 'S2.7', "analyses speedup for a parallel test system; its baseline is a dedicated machine rather than an agent's serial schedule."), ('divisible2021', 'Integrating Amdahl-like Laws and Divisible Load Theory', 'S2.7', 'integrates fixed-size and scaled speedup views; our boundary is in contention, not in problem size.'), ('workload2017', 'Workload characterization of interactive cloud services', 'S2.7', 'characterises interactive cloud workloads on two machine sizes; our workload is generated so its properties are known by construction.'), ('workload2015', 'Locality Exists in Graph Processing', 'S2.7', 'characterises graph-processing locality on a real machine; we run no real workload, which is why our ground truth is by construction.'), ('workload2024', 'Towards Cloud Efficiency with Large-scale Workload Characterization', 'S2.7', 'characterises cloud workloads at scale to improve efficiency; our contention is an instrument coordinate, not a production measurement.'), ('servegen2025', 'ServeGen', 'S2.7', 'characterises and generates LLM serving workloads; our workload is a synthetic agent loop whose parameters are all declared.'), ('hydra2026', 'Phase-Aware Workload Characterization of LLM Inference', 'S2.7', 'characterises LLM inference phases across devices; our two phases, think and tool, are separated so the speculation can be priced.'), ('stats2026', 'How to Do Statistical Evaluations in ECE/CS Papers', 'S2.7', 'gives a practical playbook for statistical evaluation; we follow it with per-seed intervals and a declared pairing rule.'), ('roofline2026', 'Cache-Aware Roofline Model Automatic Benchmarking', 'S2.7', 'automates roofline benchmarking; our instrument reports its own resolution rather than a peak.'), ('vectorproc2023', 'Vector-Processing for Mobile Devices: Benchmark and Analysis', 'S2.7', "benchmarks vector processing on mobile devices; our claim is about a mechanism's boundary rather than one platform's throughput."), ('speedupdist2024', 'Sequential Runtime Distributions for the Parallel Speedup Prediction', 'S2.7', 'predicts parallel speedup from sequential runtime distributions; we predict a crossover from a measured contention coordinate.'), ('exp2024', 'Multi-level projection with exponential parallel speedup', 'S2.7', 'reports exponential parallel speedup for a projection method; it is the kind of isolated speedup claim our serial baseline re-prices.'), ('superlinear1987', 'A note on superlinear speedup', 'S2.7', 'explains when speedups exceed the processor count; we show a series of speedups all bought by the same parallelism.'), ('model1997', 'A Model for Speedup of Parallel Programs', 'S2.7', 'models parallel speedup from program structure; our structure is a think phase and a call phase sharing a pool.'), ('linearspeedup2005', 'Scheduling parallel jobs with linear speedup', 'S2.7', 'schedules parallel jobs that speed up linearly; our jobs are single-threaded and the linear part comes from issuing them early.'), ('fixedsize2011', 'Fixed-Size Speedup', 'S2.7', 'defines fixed-size speedup as a metric; our ratio is taken at fixed work, which is that definition.'), ('unconv2019', 'Unconventional Wisdom: Superlinear Speedup', 'S2.7', 'explains superlinear speedup by search-space effects; our speedups come from overlapping waits, which is a different source.'), ('anotherview1990', 'Another view on parallel speedup', 'S2.7', 're-examines how parallel speedup should be measured; we adopt a paired per-seed ratio over the serial schedule.'), ('dlt2025', 'DLT-Aware Performance Evaluation Framework for Virtual-Core Speedup', 'S2.7', 'builds a performance-evaluation framework for virtual-core speedup; we use a deterministic simulator with ground truth by construction.'), ('util2024', 'Efficient Workload Distribution for Sustainable Server Utilization', 'S2.7', 'distributes workload for sustainable server utilisation; our utilisation is derived from busy time and makespan, not assumed.'), ('forkjoin2026', 'From Fork-Join to Asynchronous Tasks', 'S2.7', 'parallelises a tiled decomposition from fork-join to asynchronous tasks; our structure is one agent with an early-issued call.'), ('moldable2023', 'Improved Online Scheduling of Moldable Task Graphs', 'S2.7', 'schedules moldable task graphs online under a speedup function; our width is fixed per run and the schedule is what varies.'), ('variance2023', 'Blockwise Stochastic Variance-Reduced Methods with Parallel Speedup', 'S2.7', 'reports parallel speedup for a variance-reduced optimiser; its parallelism is a numerical property, ours is an issue policy.'), ('latencyhiding1993', 'Empirical study of latency hiding on a fine-grain parallel processor', 'S2.1', 'measures latency hiding empirically on a fine-grain processor; we measure it in an agent loop where the hidden unit is a tool call.'), ('optimistic2002', 'Latency Hiding with Optimistic Computations', 'S2.1', 'hides latency by computing optimistically and rolling back; our rollback has a cost on a shared pool and we vary it.'), ('memdep2005', 'Exploiting Load/Store Parallelism via Memory Dependence Prediction', 'S2.1', 'predicts memory dependences to expose parallelism; our prediction is of which call comes next, and its accuracy is an oracle.')]
